  "_doc": "What the regional style of a city changes in its roads, laid over this table by DataTables (data_tables.gd): prices and structure replace the table's, a block under profiles is laid over the profile of that id, and marking_style is the paint standard of streets.json markings.styles a new city starts with. prices: money per m2 of each part of the cross-section. roadcraft: modelling choices, the balance of the game. brasil: carriageway from DNIT, Custos Medios Gerenciais, Anexo IX, base July 2016, single carriageway, 3.6 m lanes and 2.5 m shoulders, mean R$ 3,241,000 per km over a 12.2 m platform; median and footway have no source and stay modelling choices; it paints CONTRAN's norm (br_norm). eua and europa: prices and structure are roadcraft's, no published price per m2 read for them. eua: lanes of 11 ft on local streets and 12 ft on urban streets and avenues (AASHTO Green Book 2018, 5.3.3.1 and 6.2.2.1: 10 to 12 ft), footways of 5 ft (AASHTO Guide for the Planning, Design and Operation of Pedestrian Facilities 2021, 3.2.3; PROWAG R302.3 asks 4 ft at least), MUTCD markings (us). europa: lanes of 3.25 m on urban streets and avenues and 2.75 m on local streets (RASt 06, FGSV, 6.1.1.1 and table 7: a local street of 5.50 m), footways of 2.50 m (RASt 06 4.7: 2.50 m the least side room), the white lines of the Vienna Convention (eu). structure: price multiplier by how the road is built, modelling choices in all (no published ratio found). Also modelling choices, in tuning.json: economy.start_money, refund_share, fill_from_m and on_piers_from_m.",
